# ALTERNATIVE to Cloudflare Tunnel (the recommended setup — see the README): serve
# newsletter.emnudge.dev straight from the VPS with the DNS record NOT proxied
# (grey cloud), and set CLIENT_IP_HEADER=x-forwarded-for in the service's .env.
#
# Reverse-proxy for newsletter.emnudge.dev -> the service on 127.0.0.1:8787.
# Caddy provisions and renews TLS automatically (Let's Encrypt).
#
# SECURITY — X-Forwarded-For: the service reads the *rightmost* XFF entry (the one
# a trusted proxy appends) for all per-IP guards (rate limits, per-IP caps,
# admin brute-force throttle). Caddy's reverse_proxy APPENDS the real client IP to
# whatever the client sent, so a client can prefill bogus leftmost entries — that's
# why the service ignores them. To be doubly safe we also OVERWRITE the header here
# with only the real remote host, so the service sees exactly one trustworthy value.
# Do NOT remove `header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}`: without it, a client can
# still influence the header (the service's rightmost-read defends against this, but
# defense in depth matters for the guard the whole service depends on).
#
# Install (one option): append this block to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (or drop it in
# a file that your Caddyfile imports), then:
#   sudo systemctl reload caddy

newsletter.emnudge.dev {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787 {
		header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
	}
}
